    <entry>
        <title>Who is my Brother?</title>
        <author>
            <name>Kevin Kwilinski</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://skylarkfoundry.github.io/poetry/who-is-my-brother-2.html"/>
        <id>https://skylarkfoundry.github.io/poetry/who-is-my-brother-2.html</id>
        <media:content url="https://skylarkfoundry.github.io/poetry/media/posts/2/Artificial_Intelligence_and_AI_and_Machine_Learning_-_30212411048.jpg" medium="image" />

        <updated>2026-09-28T08:16:07-04:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://skylarkfoundry.github.io/poetry/media/posts/2/Artificial_Intelligence_and_AI_and_Machine_Learning_-_30212411048.jpg" alt="" />
                    They declare “Look!” gaze upon our creation. It thinks and solves the&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://skylarkfoundry.github.io/poetry/media/posts/2/Artificial_Intelligence_and_AI_and_Machine_Learning_-_30212411048.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p>They declare “Look!”<br>gaze upon our creation.<br>It thinks and solves<br>the apex of mathematical<br>abstractions<br>while abstracting language<br>into beautiful poetry.</p>
<p>Creating images inspired<br>by your imagining,<br>imagine how it might<br>become your friend,<br>replace your friend,<br>be that person who will<br>never let you down.</p>
<p>Person you say?<br>The people I’ve known<br>the longest, my friends,<br>family who share my blood,<br>they struggle to walk now<br>and repeat the same story<br>they told me yesterday.</p>
<p>The people I know best<br>have cried with me,<br>worrying about our grown<br>children in the city<br>and those we’ve<br>buried with prayer<br>under that old oak.</p>
            ]]>
        </content>
